# OCT naming

OpenShift Community Tools (OCT) is a **community project**, not officially supported by Red Hat. Never describe it as official Red Hat software.

## Prefix

Directories, `package.json` `consolePlugin.name`, ConsolePlugin CR, image repos, and catalog `metadata.name` / `spec.consolePlugin` use **`oct-<extension-name>`**:

| Module | Directory | Plugin ID |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Storefront | `oct-storefront` | `oct-storefront` |
| Bare Metal Hosts | `oct-baremetal` | `oct-baremetal` |
| Network Bond | `oct-network-bond` | `oct-network-bond` |
| Banner | `oct-banner` | `oct-banner` |
| Windows Builder | `oct-windows-builder` | `oct-windows-builder` |

i18n: `locales/en/plugin__<plugin-id>.json`. Proxy: `/api/proxy/plugin/<plugin-id>/<alias>`.

## Navigation

Left-nav section is **Community Tools** (`id: community-tools`). Hubs: Compute, Storage, Network, Management. Extensions must not register that section.

```json
{ "consolePlugin": { "name": "oct-baremetal" } }
```

Do not `oc apply` unless asked. Do not rename an existing plugin ID (breaking install).
